    "headline_finding": {
      "active": true,
      "title": "Error-independence complementarity: refuted at scale",
      "summary": "Joint sweeps show LBPH and SFace false-accepts are positively associated (Yule's Q > 0 on every leg where estimable): they fail on the same hard impostor pairs. The cascade still wins on FAR (98 ppm on LFW1, undercutting both engines) via the gate plus AND-composition, not via error independence. The paper now reports this in §4.5. The cross-dataset overlays add a nuance: the correlation decorrelates as inputs degrade (obs/exp 12.85x on clean LFW, 2.02x light, 1.28x medium), so robustness and complementarity testing measure different things.\n",
      "source_doc": "docs/audits/STATE-07-10.md"
    }
